  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Khoisan ethnic minorities on Farmers&apos; field school, food security and reproductive health.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The empowerment of families from the Khoisan ethnic minorities, through training in environmental education, so that they can become self-producers in family farming, guaranteeing their food security and consolidating their sedentary lifestyle. Reduce their surviving style based on relying on donations, hunting and gathering strange fruits in the forest without taking into account the factors of drought and climate change. Benefiting 100 people through educational activities, total of 20 families. The project will be implemented in the province of Cuando Cubango.</narrative>
  </description>
